## 2. Authentication

| Endpoint | Method | Auth Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `/auth/register` | POST | ❌ | Create new account |
| `/auth/login` | POST | ❌ | Get access + refresh tokens |
| `/auth/me` | GET | ✅ | Get current logged-in user |
| `/auth/refresh` | POST | ❌ | Get new access token |
| `/auth/send-otp` | POST | ❌ | Send OTP to email |
| `/auth/verify-otp` | POST | ❌ | Verify OTP code |
| `/auth/change-password` | POST | ✅ | Change password |
| `/auth/logout` | POST | ✅ | Logout current session |

### Register — Request Body

```json
{
  "name": "string (required)",
  "email": "string (required, unique)",
  "password": "string (required, min 6 chars)",
  "phone": "string (optional)"
}
```

> ⚠️ Do **not** send a `role` field. All mobile app users are automatically assigned the `USER` role.

### Token Refresh

When a request returns `401 Unauthorized`, your `accessToken` has expired. Silently refresh it:

```http
POST https://api.metagod.in/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "<stored_refresh_token>"
}
```

Returns a new `accessToken`. Update your stored token and retry the original request.

### OTP Flow (Forgot Password / Verify Email)

```http
POST /api/auth/send-otp
{ "email": "arjun@example.com" }

POST /api/auth/verify-otp
{ "email": "arjun@example.com", "otp": "123456" }
```

