## 4. Error Handling

| HTTP Code | Meaning | What to do |
|---|---|---|
| `200` | OK | Use `data` normally |
| `201` | Created | Resource was created successfully |
| `400` | Bad Request | Check your request body for missing/invalid fields |
| `401` | Unauthorized | Token missing or expired → refresh token |
| `403` | Forbidden | Access denied |
| `404` | Not Found | Resource doesn't exist |
| `409` | Conflict | Duplicate entry (e.g. email already registered) |
| `500` | Server Error | Report to backend team with request details |

