## 18. Live Streaming (HLS)

### Check if Temple is Live

```http
GET /api/temples/:id
```

Check `isLive: true` in the response before showing the stream.

### Get Stream URL

```http
GET /api/temples/:id/live
```

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "isLive": true,
    "hlsUrl": "/streams/sk_shivmandir_a1b2/master.m3u8",
    "streamUrls": {
      "mainCam": "https://...",
      "sideCam": "",
      "altarCam": ""
    }
  }
}
```

### Playing HLS with `react-native-video`

```javascript
import Video from 'react-native-video';

const SERVER_URL = 'https://api.metagod.in'; // NO /api here

<Video
  source={{ uri: `${SERVER_URL}${temple.hlsUrl}` }}
  resizeMode="contain"
  paused={false}
  controls={true}
  style={{ width: '100%', height: 240 }}
/>
```

> ⚠️ `hlsUrl` is a **relative path** — prepend the server base URL **without `/api`**.  
> Example: `http://localhost:4000` + `/streams/sk_.../master.m3u8`

### Polling for Live Status

Poll every 30 seconds to check if a temple goes live:

```javascript
useEffect(() => {
  const interval = setInterval(async () => {
    const res = await axios.get(`/api/temples/${templeId}`);
    setIsLive(res.data.data.isLive);
  }, 30000);
  return () => clearInterval(interval);
}, [templeId]);
```

